    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.83,
      "end_seconds": 193.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "sit still for a moment.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.08,
      "end_seconds": 223.73,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 82 beats a minute, saturation 97 percent, temp 36.8 degrees, blood pressure 125 over 80, respiratory rate 18."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.38,
      "end_seconds": 225.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.54,
      "end_seconds": 231.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "alright, they help me see the whole picture, more shortly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.44,
      "end_seconds": 235.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.53,
      "end_seconds": 238.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "nearly finished here"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.05,
      "end_seconds": 254.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "your tummy is soft and your weight is stable on the scales"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.86,
      "end_seconds": 260.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "thank you, you can get dressed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.89,
      "end_seconds": 295.9,
      "duration_seconds": 17.01,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, it points towards coeliac disease on a gluten-free diet with some accidental exposure. Another possibility is iron deficiency. I'd like to arrange coeliac antibodies for coeliac follow-up. I think a blood count makes sense here, for coeliac follow-up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.32,
      "end_seconds": 301.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "let me think, is that done today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.71,
      "end_seconds": 324.86,
      "duration_seconds": 23.15,
      "text": "Check labels carefully and use separate toasters and chopping boards. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. I think the dietitian should see you too. See me again in twelve months. Alright, how would you describe the plan, so we're on the same page?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 326.3,
      "end_seconds": 331.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "So, I come back in twelve months. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.62,
      "end_seconds": 337.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.9,
      "end_seconds": 343.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Uh, uh, thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
